        "type": "markdown-mermaid",
        "title": "Turning points in the Pahlavi period",
        "content": "```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  A[\"1921: Reza Khan rises through a coup\"] -->|\"Chronological succession\"| B[\"1925: Reza Shah begins his reign\"]\n  B -->|\"Chronological succession\"| C[\"1941: Abdication and succession of Mohammad Reza Shah\"]\n  C -->|\"Chronological succession\"| D[\"1951: Oil nationalization under Mosaddegh\"]\n  D -->|\"Chronological succession\"| E[\"1953: Coup overthrows Mosaddegh\"]\n  E -->|\"Chronological succession\"| F[\"1979: Monarchy collapses\"]\n```",
        "summary": "The arrows indicate chronological order, not a claim that each event alone caused the next. The sequence distinguishes the dynasty’s foundation, the succession, the oil crisis, and the monarchy’s overthrow. [s1][s3][s4]",
        "as_of_date": null,
